# #1293: every pattern below (except `docs`, see its own comment) is `**/`-
# prefixed for the same reason `.vinext`/`.output` needed it below — Docker's
# `.dockerignore` matching is NOT recursive the way `.gitignore`'s is. A bare
# pattern here matches ONLY at the context root; each of these directories
# ALSO exists nested under `apps/*` and `packages/*` (e.g.
# `apps/file-manager/node_modules`, `apps/docs/.next`, `packages/kn-next/dist`,
# every workspace's own `.turbo`/`coverage`), and a bare line left every one
# of those nested copies reachable by `COPY . .` — a bloated build context, a
# HOST build's stale `.next`/`dist` output shadowing what the in-image build
# regenerates, and non-reproducible builds keyed on whatever happened to be on
# the host filesystem at build time. Audited every `COPY` in
# `apps/file-manager/Dockerfile` and `apps/docs/Dockerfile{,.oke}` (the two
# apps whose build context resolves to this workspace root — see the
# `**/.vinext` comment below) before widening: none of them `COPY`s a nested
# `node_modules`/`dist`/`.next`/`.open-next`/`.turbo`/`coverage`/`*.log` from
# the HOST context (every `COPY --from=<stage>` reads from a PREVIOUS BUILD
# STAGE's filesystem, which `.dockerignore` never touches; every non-`--from`
# `COPY` in those two Dockerfiles is `COPY . .` itself, at the very start,
# before any in-image build has produced these directories) — so widening
# every one of them to `**/` is a pure win, not a risk. Mutation-provable at
# `tests/dockerignore-recursive-pins.test.ts`.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/.open-next
**/.git
**/.turbo
**/*.log
**/coverage

# `docs` is the ONE pattern here that must stay BARE, not `**/`-prefixed —
# the opposite call from every pattern above. This line means "exclude the
# workspace ROOT's own `docs/` directory" (this repo's ADR/knowledge-base
# tree, irrelevant to any app image and worth keeping out of the build
# context). `apps/docs` is a real Next.js app — its directory is also named
# `docs`, and `apps/docs/Dockerfile`'s `COPY . .` needs it. `**/docs` would
# match `apps/docs` too (`**/` matches zero-or-more leading directories, so
# it matches any path ENDING in `/docs`, not just a root-level one) and
# silently empty the build context for that app's own Dockerfile — the
# opposite of "tidier context", an unbuildable image. Verified: `apps/docs`
# is the only other `docs`-named directory under a build-context root in this
# repo today; if a `packages/*/docs` or similar is ever added, it survives
# this pattern too, by the same reasoning.
docs

# #1284: this is the file Docker ACTUALLY reads for apps/file-manager's build
# (the CLI's `requireBuildContext` resolves the build context to the
# workspace ROOT — where a lockfile marker is found above the app — so the
# per-app apps/file-manager/.dockerignore is NOT the file that gates
# `docker build`'s context here; this one is). `.vinext/fonts/<hash>/style.css`
# caches a self-hosted next/font/google file by an ABSOLUTE FILESYSTEM PATH
# computed at fetch time (vinext's createGoogleFontsPlugin). `kn-next deploy`/
# `kn-next build` run the app's own `vite build` on the HOST before the Docker
# build; without this exclusion that HOST-path cache rides `COPY . .` into the
# image, and the in-image `RUN vite build` (apps/file-manager/Dockerfile) hits
# a CACHE HIT on the stale style.css — vinext returns it verbatim, and its
# rewrite-to-a-served-URL step only fires when the cached path matches the
# CURRENT build's cacheDir, so the HOST path leaks straight into the served
# page.
#
# MUST be `**/.vinext`, not a bare `.vinext`. Unlike `.gitignore`, a bare
# `.dockerignore` pattern matches ONLY at the context root — it does NOT
# recurse into subdirectories the way a bare gitignore pattern does. Proved
# with a minimal reproduction (a nested `subdir/.vinext/` survived a bare
# `.vinext` line and was excluded once the pattern became `**/.vinext`), and
# the app's own `.vinext` lives at `apps/file-manager/.vinext` — one level
# below this file — so a bare line here would have compiled, looked correct,
# and silently done nothing. (#1293, RESOLVED: the same gap in every OTHER
# bare pattern in this file — `node_modules`, `.next`, `.turbo`, `dist`,
# `coverage`, `*.log`, `.git` — was fixed at the top of this file; `docs` is
# the one deliberate exception, see its own comment there. Don't re-flag
# this as outstanding.)
#
# Proved end-to-end with a real `docker build` of the UNMODIFIED Dockerfile:
# WITHOUT this exclusion (even with the bare, non-recursive `.vinext` line),
# the served HTML still referenced the host checkout's own
# `.vinext/fonts/...` path (404s) — confirmed by exec'ing into the builder
# stage and finding `/repo/apps/file-manager/.vinext` present with the HOST's
# absolute path baked into its cached style.css. WITH the `**/` prefix, that
# directory does not reach the builder stage at all, the in-image `vite
# build` fetches the font fresh, and every font reference in the served HTML
# resolved to `/_next/static/_vinext_fonts/...`, serving 200 `font/woff2`.
**/.vinext

# Same staleness class as `.vinext` above: `.output` is the HOST build's
# output tree. The Dockerfile runs its own `vite build` and does not read a
# pre-existing `.output`, so excluding it costs nothing and removes another
# host-build artifact from the context. Also needs the `**/` prefix for the
# same reason.
**/.output
